<newsitem itemid="718514" id="root" date="1997-07-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: KLOOF Q2 PRE-CAPEX NET 17.15 MLN RAND.</title>
<headline>KLOOF Q2 PRE-CAPEX NET 17.15 MLN RAND.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus</p>
<p>preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending 17.15 vs 54.63</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 76.60 vs 60.11</p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    - Kloof				  5,571.9 vs 4,851.4</p>
<p>    - Leeudoorn			    1,769.1 vs 1,892.5</p>
<p>    - Libanon				2,391.5 vs 2,635.0</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    - Kloof				  465,000 vs 440,000</p>
<p>    - Leeudoorn			    285,000 vs 305,000</p>
<p>    - Libanon				402,000 vs 425,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    - Kloof				     12.0 vs 11.0   </p>
<p>    - Leeudoorn				  6.2 vs 6.2    </p>
<p>    - Libanon				    5.9 vs 6.2    </p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - Kloof				   41,180 vs 45,614 </p>
<p>    - Leeudoorn			     65,909 vs 55,020 </p>
<p>    - Libanon				 51,550 vs 46,450</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - Kloof				   49,508 vs 51,438 </p>
<p>    - Leeudoorn			     49,324 vs 52,042 </p>
<p>    - Libanon				 49,652 vs 51,668</p>
<p>Full name: Kloof Gold Mining Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE:</p>
<p>* Kloof - An increase in underground production at an</p>
<p>improved yield resulted in higher gold production. Good progress</p>
<p>continues to be made with the development towards the reef at</p>
<p>No. 4 sub-vertical shaft.</p>
<p>* Leeudoorn - Underground production was adversely affected</p>
<p>by seismicity which resulted in a shortage of payable face.</p>
<p>* Libanon - The anticipated drop in the yield occurred and</p>
<p>now reflects the expected norm</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
